<title>USA: CUNO Inc Q4 loss vs profit.</title>
<headline>CUNO Inc Q4 loss vs profit.</headline>
<dateline>MERIDEN, Conn. 1996-12-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>CUNO INC AND SUBSIDIARIES</p>
<p>			    TWELVE MONTHS ENDED  THREE MONTHS ENDED</p>
<p> (Thousands of dollars)    October 31,		October 31,</p>
<p>					1996     1995	1996    1995</p>
<p> Net sales		    $179,068 $162,699   $44,432 $41,889</p>
<p> Operating income	     17,470   10,840     3,718   3,505</p>
<p>Foreign currency</p>
<p>	gains (losses)	   (171)    (449)	(69)   (219)</p>
<p>Net income before</p>
<p>   special charges	    10,451    6,101     1,843   2,025</p>
<p>Distribution and</p>
<p>other nonrecurring</p>
<p>   costs (net of taxes) (a)  4,858	  0     1,982	 0</p>
<p> Net income			5,593    6,101     (139)   2,025</p>
<p>Earnings per common share:</p>
<p>Net income before</p>
<p>	 special charges (b).    .77	.45	 .14     .15</p>
<p>     Net income		    .41	.45     (.01)     .15</p>
<p>(a) -- Formal filings with the Securities and Exchange Commission will include CUNO's distribution and other nonrecurring costs as a component of operating expense.</p>
<p>(b) -- Including proforma interest and tax expenses to account for the allocation of $30 million in parent company debt to CUNO as a result of the distribution, EPS for Fiscal 1996 and 1995 would be $.70 and $.34, respectively.</p>
